-- title:
--   GPY ratio threshold: crossing forces two primes in one translate (conditional)
-- statement:
--   CONDITIONAL THEOREM. If the S1 main term plus its lambda-mass error lies strictly below the S2 singular-sum main term minus its three-piece error (BV endpoints + lambda-mass times k + twice the monomial error), then some translate carries primes at two distinct coordinates. The crossing inequality is a HYPOTHESIS of this theorem: it is assumed, not established, here. Also conditional on the monomial-evaluation hypotheses hMono and the divisor-weighted BV hypotheses hDiv, neither discharged here. No verdict about crossing at BV level 1/2 is claimed: the singular-sum evaluation, defect smallness, and li asymptotics needed to decide crossing are not proved here.
-- source:
--   GPY ratio analysis: threshold, main-term approximations, and BV level cap

